DO NOT GET INVOLVED WITH WHY UNIFIED — THEY WILL SCAM YOU.
Here’s exactly what happened to me, and this is the letter I sent to the BBB trying to get my money back:
I signed a contract with Why Unified on June 28, 2024 for their “done-for-you” Amazon store. Two days later, I paid $13,724 by check. 
Their contract clearly states that if I’m unhappy at the end of the one-year term (June 28, 2025), I can cancel and get a full refund.
Well, over that entire year they tried selling three products for me — not a single sale came in. Every time I asked for real numbers 
or guidance, I’d get vague lines like “you’re close to the necessary metrics,” but never any actual data.
Meanwhile, Amazon charged me $39.99/month until December 2024… when the charges suddenly stopped. That’s how I discovered my store 
had quietly been deactivated. No notice, no explanation.
Before my contract ended, I emailed their Compliance Department to cancel and request my refund exactly as the contract allows. 
It’s been over 30 days since then — endless follow-up calls, but no answers. 
They keep telling me I have to wait for a “compliance portal” that still isn’t functional. Compliance doesn’t answer 
calls or emails, and apparently they don’t have a phone number.
I requested a full refund of $13,963.94 (my payment + Amazon fees) just as the contract promises.
Their response to my BBB complaint?
They said everything must go through their “secure Compliance Dashboard” — which, conveniently, I can’t access because 
my identity is “still being verified.” Their own page says it only takes 1–2 business days. 
It has now been a full month since October 30th, and I still have no access, no updates, no contact, no resolution.
It is now November 30, 2025 — and I’ve heard absolutely nothing.
So yes — based on my experience, this company is a scam, and 
I’m going to keep posting my story anywhere I can to warn people before they lose money like I did.
If you're wondering whether to invest with Why Unified:
Don’t!  Run.
I wish someone had warned me the way I’m warning you now.
